<h1>Lesson 5: JS Functions, Conditionals, and Loops</h1>

<div style="display: inline-block; background-color: #E4E2F8; color: #1F1976; font-weight: bold; padding: 4px 12px; border-radius: 10px; margin-bottom: 12px;">Aligns to curriculum Lessons 9-11</div>

<p>This lesson prepares you to teach three curriculum lessons:</p>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 10px;">
<p><b>Curriculum Lesson 9:</b> Writing Reusable Functions</p>
<a href="[LESSON 9 URL]" style="display: inline-block; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 13px;">View Curriculum Lesson 9</a>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 10px;">
<p><b>Curriculum Lesson 10:</b> Making Decisions with If/Else</p>
<a href="[LESSON 10 URL]" style="display: inline-block; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 13px;">View Curriculum Lesson 10</a>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 16px;">
<p><b>Curriculum Lesson 11:</b> Loops and Counted Repetition</p>
<a href="[LESSON 11 URL]" style="display: inline-block; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 13px;">View Curriculum Lesson 11</a>
</div>

<hr>

<p><b>In this lesson, you'll:</b></p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 6px 0;">• Step through defining and calling a function, panel by panel</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 6px 0;">• Compare named and anonymous functions, and see abstraction in action</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 6px 0;">• Trace a flowchart's decision diamond into a working if/else, live</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 6px 0;">• Run a real for loop and watch start, stop, and step control its output</p>
<p style="margin: 0;">• Diagnose a genuine off-by-one bug using the Loop Debugging Checklist</p>

<div style="background-color: #E4E2F8; color: #222222; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 16px 0;">
<p><b>💡 Notice as you explore:</b> how a checklist can flag that something's wrong without actually diagnosing why, and that the debugging skill worth teaching is knowing the difference.</p>
</div>

<hr>

